A||||7||Richard Parnell||Firewall Protection||||11
Z||000000||Richard Parnell||09-27-1999||03:47 PM||||I've read of the 4 cyl engine throwing rods and occasionally the trannys blowing on Fieros.  Is the firewall enough protection for the driver and passenger in case something blows?  I ask because I'm planning some major "souping up" on my '87 SC.||||reg||11
Z||000001||Patrick||09-27-1999||03:52 PM||||<BR>You might want to put on a "jock" with a steel cup before you rev 'er to ten grand. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||10
Z||000002||theogre||09-27-1999||07:07 PM||||the 4 cyl block will not take large amounts of abuse from performance upgrades. put in a 6 if you want to do that kind of thing.<P>There is only a limited amount you can do to a DIS motor.<P>1. it is not compatible with the improved holley design 300 TBI.<P>2. Accell makes the only after market coils.<P>3. MSD makes the only after market ignition enhancement. I say enhancement because it is placed, electrically, between the coils and the controller brick. Cutting the factory harness is required.<P>4. the motor block will not take large displacement or compression increases. It will break rather easily.<P>5. the stock rods are know for breaking. It's one reason the thing redlines at 4500.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||09-27-1999||09:08 PM||||Blowing and engine is mostly a figure of speech.  Rarely does one actually blow up except in race engines with exotic fuel.<BR>I wouldn't worry too much about the strength of the firewall.<P>Take care,<BR>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000004||Eddie||09-27-1999||09:21 PM||||Hay leave it stock trust me I have $3500.00 into my motor and I should have JUST GOT A V6 	<BR>  for ever sorry Eddie||||reg||1
Z||000005||Racer 1||09-28-1999||01:36 AM||||My 4 cyld Iron Duck has 206,000 miles on it and still going strong. I wear fire retardent clothes like dragster people wear. Just incase if the engine catches on fire thats a hell alot of plastic burning around you. ||||reg||5
Z||000006||Cliff Pennock||09-28-1999||03:40 AM||||I blew up the engine of a BMW 7 series once. That engine literally <B>blew up</B>! It died on me on the highway and after it had stopped I opened the hood to see what was wrong. When I tried to start it again, I heared a <I>very</I> loud bang... I found the valve cover about 30 yards away and the explosion had just about ripped the engine in two!||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||09-28-1999||09:32 AM||||I've seen the early versions of this motor put rods thru the block. This specific problem is part of the reason for the full sheild between the block and exhaust. the sheild also deflects oil from failed valve cover gaskets away from the manifold. the 84 had oil distribution problems that were improved from 85 on, but the motor is still not anything but what it originally was....... An economy motor easy on emmisions and fuel consumption.||||reg||1
